# Both stacks run on Linux. Pin LF so it stays that way no matter which OS commits, and
# regardless of the committer's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# This is prevention, not a fix for an existing problem — the tree is already all-LF. But a
# CRLF file reaching the Linux host fails in ways that are genuinely hard to read:
#   *.sh   -> bash sees `set -uo pipefail\r`, and every string comparison carries a stray \r
#   *.env* -> Compose reads the \r into the value, so ${VAULT_HOST_PATH} becomes a mount
#             path ending in a carriage return and the container refuses to start
#   *.py   -> shebang lines and PEP 723 inline metadata blocks stop being recognised
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures are real documents — never transform them.
*.pdf  binary
*.doc  binary
*.docx binary
*.xls  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.ppt  binary
*.pptx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.zip  binary
